bindgen 0.71.1: follow a type's definition, as clang 22 no longer does

clang 22 makes clang_getTypeDeclaration() return the forward declaration
of a struct where older releases returned its definition, so bindgen
emitted opaque structs (a lone `_address` field) for the PostgreSQL
headers and pgrx-pg-sys failed to compile.

Backport of the fix released in bindgen 0.72.1:
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen/issues/3278
https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen/commit/2e06749639

pgrx-bindgen 0.16.1 requires bindgen ^0.71.1, so the fixed release cannot
be vendored. Drop this patch once pgvectorscale moves to a pgrx that
pulls bindgen >= 0.72.1.

--- a/vendor/bindgen-0.71.1/clang.rs
+++ b/vendor/bindgen-0.71.1/clang.rs
@@ -1213,11 +1213,11 @@
 
     /// Get a cursor pointing to this type's declaration.
     pub(crate) fn declaration(&self) -> Cursor {
-        unsafe {
-            Cursor {
-                x: clang_getTypeDeclaration(self.x),
-            }
-        }
+        let decl = Cursor {
+            x: unsafe { clang_getTypeDeclaration(self.x) },
+        };
+        // Prior to clang 22, the declaration pointed to the definition.
+        decl.definition().unwrap_or(decl)
     }
 
     /// Get the canonical declaration of this type, if it is available.
